"An @error handler written without its kind. handler is a non-null enum, so the application is illegal against the definition: assembly reports it, and capture records the element as undecoded rather than writing a row its kind column refuses. Before that guard the refused insert failed the capture of the whole corpus, every other document in the store included."
type Refused @table(name: "film") @error(handlers: [{className: "java.lang.IllegalStateException"}]) {
  id: ID
}

extend type Query {
  refused: Refused
}

extend schema @assertContains(relation: "graphitron_undecoded_argument_entry", rows: """
  directive_name, directive_argument_name
  error,          handlers
  """)

# The illegal application is refused at the entry grain as well: no decode, so no handler rows.
extend schema @assertEmpty(relation: "graphitron_ast_error_entry", where: "1 = 1")

# The schema problem assembly reports, which is where an illegal application belongs.
extend schema @expectEquals(relation: "graphql_schema_problem", rows: """
  stage,    error_class
  ASSEMBLY, DirectiveIllegalArgumentTypeError
  """)
